<title>USA: Cascade Q1 revenues hurt by uneven buying.</title>
<headline>Cascade Q1 revenues hurt by uneven buying.</headline>
<dateline>WESTFORD, Mass. 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cascade Communications Corp said its revenues for the first quarter of 1997 fell short of analysts' expectations due to uneven buying patterns and variations in the timing of its customers'  network expansions.</p>
<p>Cascade, a maker of switching products used by public carriers and Internet service providers, gave the explanation as it reported first quarter 1997 revenue of $90.3 million.</p>
